{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"agent_message","text":"The proposal contract requires callers to advance the session after successful completion; retrying that completed series to demonstrate cache corruption would violate the contract. Output-buffer mutation rights are still unresolved, so an aliasing test would not settle applicability. Separately, proposal input reuse is protected by copying during encoding, and session snapshot code saves and restores eviction order. I’ll retain those explanations and move on.\n"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python - <<'PY'\nimport json\ns=dict(action='research',rationale='Retain contract investigation and distinguish unsupported result-buffer mutation from explicitly protected proposal input reuse; do not spend an execution on a scenario whose caller legality is unsettled.',sources=[dict(id='M-propose-session-contract',file='nodehost.go',start_line=554,end_line=571,kind='interface_statement'),dict(id='M-async-propose-contract',file='nodehost.go',start_line=811,end_line=830,kind='interface_statement'),dict(id='M-propose-copy-entry',file='request.go',start_line=1057,end_line=1109,kind='code_observation'),dict(id='M-encode-copy',file='internal/rsm/encoded.go',start_line=70,end_line=109,kind='code_observation'),dict(id='M-lru-snapshot',file='internal/rsm/lrusession.go',start_line=87,end_line=169,kind='code_observation'),dict(id='M-lru-order-test',file='internal/rsm/lrusession_test.go',start_line=94,end_line=194,kind='test_expectation'),dict(id='M-snapshot-session-buffer',file='internal/rsm/statemachine.go',start_line=607,end_line=634,kind='code_observation')],feedback=dict(ref_ids=['surface:RequestResult.GetResult / Session.addResponse','B-apply','M-propose-session-contract','M-async-propose-contract','M-client-result','M-result-data','M-session-response','M-propose-copy-entry','M-encode-copy','M-lru-snapshot','M-lru-order-test','M-snapshot-session-buffer'],answered='The synchronous and asynchronous proposal contracts explicitly distinguish timed-out retries from successful completion: on success the client must call ProposalCompleted before future proposals. Therefore obtaining a successful result, mutating its Data and then reissuing the same completed series is not an applicable retry witness. Existing shallow Result.Data propagation remains an observation, but output mutation/retention rights are still unspecified in the i